                      <p>Most advice about building an online following is written for a different game: competing for algorithmic reach among millions of strangers, where audiences can rise or fall overnight. You’re not playing that game. <br><br>Your audience is a few hundred or few thousand peers, colleagues and industry partners who already have a reason to listen to you. That makes this a smaller, slower, reputation-based market, closer to building a specialist reputation than influencer marketing. </p>
                      <p>That’s why the advice here favors fewer, better pieces for people who already know you, rather than volume and trend-chasing. It’s not caution. It’s what works in a relationship market rather than a reach market. </p>
